	<title>Five Little Peppers and How They Grew</title>
	<isbn>1416916172</isbn>
	<publication_year>2006</publication_year>
	<language_code>eng</language_code>
	<description>&lt;i&gt;Five Little Peppers and How They Grew&lt;/i&gt; was originally serialized in an 1880 edition of &lt;i&gt;Wide Awake&lt;/i&gt;, a children's magazine. The publisher of the magazine, Daniel Lothrop, loved the Pepper stories so much that he published a hard-cover edition of the story -- and married the author in 1881. In 1883 the couple moved to historic Concord, Massachusetts, and resided in a house called the Wayside, which had previously been home to Nathaniel Hawthorne and also to Louisa May Alcott, the author of &lt;i&gt;Little Women&lt;/i&gt;.</description>
